{"t": 1794113098.2975733, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*Checkout \u2014 PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731)*\n\n*Impact:* ~38% of checkout charge requests to the payment gateway returning 4xx since 07:41 UTC.\n\n*Cause:* The payment gateway moved to API version 2026-11, which enforces strict amounts: `amount` must be an integer in minor units (cents). `checkout/gateway.py` was still sending a decimal EUR amount (`{\"amount\": 12.34, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`), so charges were rejected with `400 invalid_amount` \u2014 gateway log: \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\".\n\n*Fix:* `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) before sending, e.g. 12.34 EUR -> 1234. Verified locally: 12.34 -> 1234 (int), 0.01 -> 1, 1234.56 -> 123456.\n\n*Next:* deploy the change and watch the gateway 4xx rate / `invalid_amount` log lines; they should drop to zero after rollout."}, "ok": true}
